# version and date-released track the latest GitHub release.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use The Harmonic Algorithm in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "The Harmonic Algorithm"
authors:
  - family-names: South
    given-names: Oscar
    email: oscarsouth@gmail.com
    website: "https://theHarmonicAlgorithm.com"
version: 3.1.0
date-released: 2026-08-30
repository-code: "https://github.com/OscarSouth/theHarmonicAlgorithm"
url: "https://theHarmonicAlgorithm.com"
license: GPL-3.0-only
abstract: >-
  The Harmonic Algorithm system, integrated with TidalCycles, generates
  musical harmony states inside user defined musical constraints, then ranks
  it using a tailored 'cube' of Markov Chain matrices trained on the Yale
  Classical Archives Corpus. This presents a unique tool in the hands of the
  composer or performer which can be used as a composing aid, analysis
  device, for instrumental study or even in live performance.
keywords:
  - algorithmic composition
  - generative music
  - live coding
  - TidalCycles
  - Haskell
  - Neo4j
  - music theory
  - harmony
  - orchestration
  - Markov chains
